NList.mcc/MUIA_NList_Quiet

    NAME
        MUIA_NList_Quiet -- [.S.], BOOL

    FUNCTION
        Same function as List.mui/MUIA_List_Quiet.

        Think about using it when you insert/remove several entries
        one by one, it will go much faster.
        In all cases all changes which can be done later are delayed.
        Quiet_Full mean that no notify caused by changes in the list will
        be made, while Quiet_Visual will done them (but delayed to after
        the Quiet_None).

    SPECIAL INPUTS
        MUIV_NList_Quiet_None       same as FALSE.
        MUIV_NList_Quiet_Full       all values but FALSE and MUIV_NList_Quiet_Visual (-2).
        MUIV_NList_Quiet_Visual

    SEE ALSO
        MUIM_NList_Insert, MUIM_NList_Remove
NList.mcc/MUIA_NList_SelectChange

    NAME
        MUIA_NList_SelectChange -- Receive a selection-change notification.

    INPUTS
        Notification trigger; BOOL. The local getter returns TRUE, not a
        stored selection state.

    FUNCTION
        NList emits TRUE when pending line-selection changes are delivered.
        Notifications can be coalesced by the class notification machinery;
        one notification does not identify one particular row. Use Select or
        NextSelected to inspect state.

        Setting the attribute yourself does not select entries. Character
        selection does not use all the same line-selection helper paths. For
        subclass callbacks with row and state arguments, use
        MUIM_NList_SelectChange; its default handler returns zero.

    SEE ALSO
        MUIM_NList_SelectChange, MUIM_NList_Select, MUIM_NList_NextSelected

NList.mcc/MUIA_NList_ShowDropMarks

    NAME
        MUIA_NList_ShowDropMarks -- [ISG], BOOL

